,\"CSAFPID-40\",\"CSAFPID-38\",\"CSAFPID-1\",\"CSAFPID-39\",\"CSAFPID-37\",\"CSAFPID-35\",\"CSAFPID-33\",\"CSAFPID-30\",\"CSAFPID-32\"],\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/support/advisories-notices/sa-download/?sa=85-SecurityAdvisory85_4.28_Hotfix.swix\"},{\"category\":\"mitigation\",\"details\":\"Hotfix: SecurityAdvisory85_4.29_Hotfix.swix, 1.0, Hash: (SHA-512)c965e149cbbaa8698648af9290c5a728e9fe635186eee7629b789502ef37db4a94beea5ecd20e1dc8a19c2cc8988052b625cfccf764c28b8b0e9e4eef8e79bb4\",\"product_ids\":[\"CSAFPID-44\",\"CSAFPID-42\",\"CSAFPID-43\",\"CSAFPID-45\"],\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/support/advisories-notices/sa-download/?sa=85-SecurityAdvisory85_4.29_Hotfix.swix\"}],\"scores\":[{\"cvss_v3\":{\"baseScore\":7.5,\"baseSeverity\":\"HIGH\",\"vectorString\":\"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H\",\"version\":\"3.1\"},\"products\":[\"CSAFPID-4\",\"CSAFPID-0\",\"CSAFPID-3\",\"CSAFPID-2\",\"CSAFPID-1\"]}],\"title\":\"CVE-2023-24545\"},{\"cve\":\"CVE-2023-24513\",\"id\":{\"system_name\":\"Arista Bug ID\",\"text\":\"764777\"},\"notes\":[{\"category\":\"description\",\"text\":\"On affected platforms running Arista CloudEOS a size check bypass issue in the Software Forwarding Engine (Sfe) may allow buffer over reads in later code. Additionally, depending on configured options (e.g. MSS clamping), this may cause a recomputation of the TCP checksum on a very large buffer (64KB) instead of a very small one, which could be leveraged in DDoS attacks.\\n\",\"title\":\"CVE Description\"},{\"category\":\"other\",\"text\":\"In order to be vulnerable to CVE-2023-24545 and CVE-2023-24513, the switch must be configured to run the Software Forwarding Engine (Sfe). Sfe is the default configuration on CloudEOS platforms. \\nswitch(config#show agent Sfe uptime\\nAgent Name       Restarts       Uptime\\n---------------- -------------- -------\\nSfe              1              0:29:49\\n\\n\",\"title\":\"764777: Required Config for Exploitation\"}],\"product_status\":{\"fi